{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786797033,"nonce":"aolSK4J8bxxVpDwRzfVE9OjFnpQ=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDORPa0Bs8AAAABM4WmcQ","github-url":"https://github.com/FhG-IISB/jNO/issues/99","origin":"github"},"title":"u.bounds with a coordinate-expression bound on a vector field NaNs silently","message":"## What\n\n`u.bounds(lo, hi)` documents that `lo`/`hi` may be \"a number, a coordinate expression, or a HistoryRef\". On a **vector-valued** field, a coordinate-expression bound makes the Newton solve diverge to NaN instead of either working or refusing.\n\n## Reproduction (found 2026-08-15, on `feat/tier2-contact-dirichlet`)\n\n```python\nd = jno.Shape.rect(0, 0, 1, 1, size=0.15).domain()\nu, phi = d.fem_symbols(value_shape=(2,))\nX = d.variable(\"interior\", split=True)[:2]\nxc, yc = X\neu, ep = jno.np.symgrad(u, list(X)), jno.np.symgrad(phi, list(X))\nxt, yt, _ = d.variable(\"top\", split=True)\nfem = jno.fem([\n    LAM*jno.np.trace(eu)*jno.np.trace(ep) + 2*MU*jno.np.inner(eu, ep, n_contract=2),\n    u(xt, yt)[0] - 0.0, u(xt, yt)[1] - (-0.1),\n    u.bounds(-0.05 - 10.0*yc, None),   # a \"floor\" that binds only near y=0\n])\nfem.solve(nonlinear=jno.solve.newton(line_search=True, rtol=1e-6, atol=1e-6))\n# RuntimeError: newton_krylov did not converge ... residual norm nan\n```\n\nThe constraint set is feasible (at the top Dirichlet nodes the bound evaluates to -10.05, far below the imposed -0.1), so this is not the infeasible-constraint case — a *constant* bound conflicting with a Dirichlet value also NaNs, but that one is at least a user error.\n\n## Suspected cause\n\n`_resolve_bounds` resolves `lo`/`hi` \"to DOF-space vectors\" — a scalar coordinate expression evaluated per **node** likely has length `n_nodes` while the vector field's DOF vector has length `n_nodes * vec`, so the min-map arithmetic broadcasts/misaligns. Existing tests (`tests/test_fem_bounds.py`) cover constant bounds and scalar fields only; the coordinate-expression × vector-field cell of the matrix is untested.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA spatial bound on a vector field is exactly the rigid-obstacle spelling (`uy \u003e= floor(x)`), and it is the missing oracle connecting `u.bounds` to `u.gap` contact (a flat rigid obstacle is expressible both ways; the cross-check test could not be written because of this defect — see the note in the one-sided-contact commit).\n\nEither make the resolution vector-aware (per-component or broadcast-per-node, documented), or refuse loudly with the component semantics named.","files":null}]}